# Repository Boundaries

This repository is `wiloo-app-mobile`: the Flutter client for Android, iOS, and desktop.

The historical `wiloo` platform repository owns:

- `apps/backend`: NestJS backend, Better Auth, business API, database access, guards, tenant logic, and domain rules
- `apps/frontend`: existing Next.js web application

## Source Of Truth

The backend remains the source of truth for:

- authentication and session validity
- roles and scopes
- tenant/org context
- business rules
- persistence
- API contracts
- Timeclock terminal authorization

Flutter consumes the existing backend API. Flutter does not define backend behavior.

## Allowed Here

- Flutter app code
- Flutter UI, navigation, state management, and platform integration
- Flutter DTOs and API clients aligned with backend contracts
- Flutter tests
- mobile documentation, ADRs, and Cursor rules

## Not Allowed Here

- backend endpoint implementation
- backend authentication flows
- backend guards, interceptors, or decorators
- database schema or migration changes
- custom mobile auth endpoints
- JWT systems outside Better Auth
- backend business rule rewrites
- direct changes to backend code

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- Do not touch backend code from this repository.
- Do not create backend endpoints from this repository.
- Do not generate Flutter code unless the user explicitly asks for implementation.
- Do not modify `lib/` when the user asks for documentation-only work.
- Check backend documentation, Swagger/OpenAPI, or backend contracts before creating Flutter DTOs.
- If mobile needs a backend change, document it as a backend requirement and handle it in the platform/backend repository.
